    "mother_plans": {
      "mother_plan:preparation": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "preparation",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Research an overhead-conscious parallel quicksort for the four-core ARM64 target. Keep case generation and its PRNG sequence unchanged; parallelize only after generation, using race-free pivot selection, independent partitions, and generic size/depth limits with a serial fallback. Validate the exact sorted-array MD5 and output.",
          "B": "Research a distinct parallel mergesort or chunk-sort/merge approach, using one reusable scratch buffer and bounded parallel work. Account for its extra memory and task overhead with a generic small-input fallback. Preserve generation and checksum behavior, and evaluate end-to-end rather than assuming sorting dominates.",
          "C": "Research a low-overhead, robust sequential alternative such as introsort: insertion sort for small ranges, a worst-case heapsort fallback, and a partition strategy that handles duplicates. Replace only sorting behavior; retain exact generated values, sortedness validation, and MD5 output. Compare full-run performance against the existing quicksort.",
