        "plan": {
          "A": "Use the measured A candidate f1bcac767c3c46e0 (0.00632 s) as the starting point: packed row bitsets, mapped-degree checks, and sparse lower-triangle adjacency checks. Explore safe refinements such as a global degree-multiset rejection, retaining them only if the complete program measures faster. Preserve Heap order and the reference’s exact output behavior; do not skip valid matching permutations.",
          "B": "Investigate the exact incremental-mismatch approach only as a measured, size-gated alternative to full verification. The two measured B variants were slower (0.02423 and 0.02694 s versus the 0.00842 s baseline), so diagnose their overhead rather than adopting them unconditionally. Any update must account exactly for both swapped vertices, their mutual pair, diagonals, and all affected lower-triangle pairs; compare end-to-end results against the packed-bitset candidate.",
