          "analysis": "The source exhaustively enumerates Heap permutations, verifies mappings, and has observable output behavior that must remain intact; an arbitrary single valid mapping is not a safe replacement. The strongest measured result is A’s packed-bitset verifier (0.00632 s). Degree-sequence filtering measured 0.00721 s, the contiguous-byte variant 0.00722 s, and the tested OpenMP variant 0.00913 s. Both incremental-mismatch variants were substantially slower at 0.02423–0.02694 s. These timings favor the packed-bitset approach as the integration baseline while leaving room for independently measured, sound filters."
