    "mother_plans": {
      "mother_plan:preparation": {
        "model_calls": 1,
        "phase": "preparation",
        "plan": {
          "A": "Research ID lookup elimination. Replace repeated linear find_by_id scans with an immutable ID-to-original-index table built once. Prioritize a compact open-addressed hash table; preserve the first matching record and support arbitrary integer IDs without assuming dense numbering, input order, or topological order. Handle missing IDs and collisions correctly. Initially retain the existing parser and evaluation recurrence to isolate indexing gains. Measure construction and lookup costs together against the baseline; avoid oversized tables or unconditional parallel setup. Provide a complete correct candidate and a lookup interface that B and G can reuse.",
          "B": "Research reuse of shared path suffixes. Each node deterministically selects at most one successor, so implement demand-driven successor caching and memoized costs with an explicit path stack. Follow a query until reaching a terminal or cached node, then unwind, storing each float result in exactly the original recursive addition order. Terminal nodes must return their own value unchanged, without an extra addition of zero. Use separate validity flags rather than reserving a numerical cost as an uncomputed marker. Preserve the selected-ID -1 stopping rule and do not assume IDs encode a topological order. Prefer computing only queried paths; compare eager preprocessing only if measurements justify it. Keep this evaluation layer compatible with A's lookup table.",
          "C": "Research input-processing and storage overhead. Compare the existing fscanf-based reader with buffered, line-aware input and compact contiguous storage. Parse neighbor IDs once or retain spans suitable for lazy parsing, avoiding repeated strcpy, strtok_r, and atoi work. Preserve query token spelling and ordering, record boundaries, and valid integer and floating-point syntax. Retain correctly rounded float conversion, such as strtof; do not substitute approximate decimal conversion. Measure whether eager neighbor decoding earns back its cost versus decoding only visited nodes. Keep output byte-compatible and avoid unnecessary allocation, copying, and thread startup. Coordinate the representation with B's successor cache rather than introducing redundant caches.",
          "G": "Integrate only correctness-passing programs produced by A, B, and C. Start with the best measured standalone candidate, then add compatible changes incrementally: ID lookup plus demand-driven suffix caching is the primary combination; incorporate C's reader/storage changes separately. Recheck the shared semantic contract, especially first-match lookup, neighbor ties, the -1 sentinel, float addition order, and query labels. Use only the existing correctness and end-to-end timing workflow within unchanged budgets, including parsing, preprocessing, allocation, and output costs. Record component provenance and actual combined timings; gains are not additive, and retaining a standalone winner is acceptable. Treat differences near baseline timing variation cautiously. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions, and never specialize to test values or expected outputs.",
          "analysis": "The relevant task is Problem F, Graph Search on a DAG. The source repeatedly performs O(N) ID searches, reparses neighbor strings, and recomputes shared greedy-path suffixes. These are structural optimization opportunities, not measured bottleneck attribution. This run has only a correct baseline: four correctness cases and three timings averaging 11.745 ms, ranging from 11.725 to 11.775 ms. On four ARM64 CPU cores without GPUs, prioritize work elimination and low overhead rather than assuming parallelism helps. All trees must preserve the actual greedy computation, not replace it with maximum-total-path dynamic programming: scan neighbors in listed order, ignore missing IDs, and update only when a value strictly exceeds a running maximum initialized to zero. Equal values retain the first winner; selected ID -1 stops recursion. Lookup returns the first matching record, and a missing query returns zero. Preserve recursive float rounding without reassociation or double accumulation, plus original query-token spelling, duplicates, order, and output formatting. Every valid input must remain correct."
        },
        "request_sha256": "213afda9e3ba5913d068ba331cecdefa62ef27f56b3ed11399fed4cdb50064ea",
        "response": {
