          "depth": 1,
          "epoch": 1,
          "hypothesis": "Using NEON intrinsics to compute squared distances for batches of 4 points simultaneously (via vld2q_f32 deinterleave) combined with a binary-search insertion into the sorted list reduces loop-carried dependencies and improves SIMD throughput. Prefetching upcoming cache lines further mitigates memory latency, while replacing linear scan with memmove-based shift lowers instruction count.",
