          "hypothesis": "Applying two-dimensional tiling over both rows and columns of the search loop improves temporal reuse of integral image data by keeping a tile of II in cache across multiple row and column iterations. Precomputing pointers to II rows reduces index calculation overhead, while choosing B_COL larger than B_ROW exploits sequential access along rows (row-major layout) within each tile.",
